    "result_text": "Both findings addressed; tests green.\n\n**Point 1 (import ordering) \u2014 fixed.** Moved `import ...audit.OwnerAuditEventPublisher;` out from between the `rest.dto.*` block and `service.ClinicService`, placing it at the start of the `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.*` group (right after the `org.springframework.http.*` imports, before `mapper.OwnerMapper`), restoring the file's alphabetical ordering.\n\n**Point 2 (field-derivation asymmetry) \u2014 agreed, documented.** Your read of the reason is exactly right: the `audit` package deliberately doesn't depend on `mapper`, and deriving `membershipLevel` needs `OwnerMapper`, so the caller supplies it pre-computed. I added that rationale to both `OwnerCreatedEvent.of(...)` and `OwnerAuditEventPublisher.ownerCreated(...)`, with an explicit \"do not pull the mapper in here\" note so the next maintainer doesn't \"simplify\" it into a package-cycle.\n\nI left the code structure otherwise as-is (your correctness note on return types was out of scope, and `formatMembershipLevel` does return `Integer`, matching the parameter).\n\nAcceptance test `coreEventCarriesIdAndIdentifier` still passes \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
